WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.045
The cleanest boundary is specification versus implementation.

2
00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:11.537
A RISC-V specification defines software-visible behavior: encodings, state, privilege rules, and other contracts.

3
00:00:11.537 --> 00:00:14.190
It does not force one pipeline or cache.

4
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.510
OpenHW projects make those choices.

5
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:22.213
CVE2 is a small two-stage embedded design; CVA6 is a configurable six-stage code base.

6
00:00:22.213 --> 00:00:27.385
For instructions and architectural behavior, start with RISC-V specifications.

7
00:00:27.385 --> 00:00:33.750
For timing, interfaces, configuration, or release status, use the project manual and repository.

